 have a free name  change that you haven't used yet oh and  you know the february 2022 online  blizzcon well it's been canceled however  blizzard did say despite the lack of an  event it will still be making  announcements and providing updates for  its games in that month and when it  comes to the reason for cancellation  blizzard said in part we feel the energy  it would take to put on a show like this  is best directed towards supporting our  teams and progressing development of our  games and experiences additionally we  would also like to take the time to  reimagine what a blizzcon event in the  future could look like  alright switching gears from what's been  canceled to what's been delayed  after a bit of a slow year the division  2 team has released a new road map for  the future of the game and unfortunately  for fans it pushes back the next big  update to february of 2022 during the  wait players will get more behind the  scenes updates from the dev team with  the return of the intelligence annex  series of deep dive articles into  upcoming features and changes  are you guys out there still into the  division 2 and holding out for these  updates if not what game pulled your  attention let me know in the comments  [Music]  finally some good news for pikmin fans  nintendo and niantic have announced  their next mobile app pikmin bloom  considing with the 20th anniversary of  nintendo's nature-based franchise the  game sees players enter a world of lush  green earth one where pikmin can sprout  and grow via player steps pikmin are  grown from seedlings which are planted  into a special slot in the player's  backpack so steps can be registered each  pikmin takes 1 000 steps to sprout after  which they can be pulled and become part  of the player's pikmin squad you can  also name each pikmin you pull a first  for the franchise that gives an extra  bit of personality to your pikmin  congrats to all the pikmin fans out  there this is huge news will you be  playing